  "description": "Non material amendment to planning permission 24/1113/FUL dated 22/01/2025 for 'Demolition of existing units in the central and southern parts of the existing building and construction of new replacement self-contained dwellings to provide 36 residential units (Class C3).  Alterations to the existing and retained front part of the building to provide 3 reconfigured self-contained residential units and the retention of 1 existing self-contained residential unit (Class C3), along with other general refurbishment and alterations works, new landscaping, refuse store, car and cycle parking, sub-station and retaining existing accesses on East End Road and Pulham Avenue. Retention of St Anne's House (2 units) and general refurbishment and improvement works'. Amendments include before any demolition begins, a demolition management plan must be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and before any construction begins, a construction management plan must be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority. These detailed plans should cover vehicle access and parking, site setup, environmental controls (dust, noise, vibration), and community liaison. These plans aim to ensure safety, minimise disruption, and protect air quality, in line with local and London Plan policies\"\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\r",
